A||||1||MooCow||How many diferent 3.4 engines are there????||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||08-08-2000||01:13 PM||||Okay I know this has been talked about a lot.  I even did a search on it and still can't figure it out.  How many different 3.4 liter engines are there??<BR>The one that I would like to do next year in the summer is a DOHC 3.4 from say a monta carlo.  Someone give me a web site that shows how I must move the starter and everything I need to complete this task.  <BR>Thanks so much for helping Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||08-08-2000||01:36 PM||||I count 4:<P>1. 91-95 3.4L DOHC. 91-93 was batch fire and 94-95 was sequential. Both were SD.<BR>2. 96 3.4L DOHC. New heads, intake, exhaust. Mass airflow.<BR>3. 3.4L HT upgrade/93-95 Camaro. Pushrod engine for the S10 truck and Camaro. <BR>4. 3.4L SFI 95-2000. Pushrod engine. An upgraded 3100 SFI. Mass air flow. Some roller stuff.<P>If you are doing the DOHC, the starter doesn't move. You might be thinking of the 3.4L HT upgrade. The starter has to swap to the other side. Holes must be drilled and tapped.<P>Finally, a DOHC block won't work in place of a 3.4L HT upgrade assembly. No place for the lifters.......<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-08-2000).]||||reg||1
